## Verified facts (no scores — excluded per rule)

- **Identity / name:** `mai-experimental-test` (`mai-experimental-test` dataset slug / `model/mai-experimental-test/` folder). Described by `modelcomp.vercel.app` as an "experimental Microsoft MAI sandbox slot" — not a released product SKU. No separate official Microsoft release announcement specifically for `mai-experimental-test` found in fetched official Microsoft AI docs (`microsoft.ai/news/` releases list `MAI-Thinking-1`, `MAI-Code-1-Flash`, `MAI-Image-2.5`, `MAI-Transcribe-1.5`, `MAI-Voice-2` — no `MAI-Experimental-Test` or equivalent). The closest family members are `mai-thinking-1` (reasoning, Aug 12, 2026) and `mai-code-1-flash` (coding, June 2, 2026) — both fully verified with official model cards and benchmark tables (`microsoft.ai/pdf/MAI-Thinking-1-Model-Card.PDF`, `microsoft.ai/pdf/MAI-Code-1-Flash-Model-Card.PDF`). No official benchmark card or spec page specifically for `mai-experimental-test` located.
- **Status:** Experimental / sandbox / placeholder (`modelcomp.vercel.app` description: "placeholder, not a model"; dataset `model-queue.md` includes it at Overall 46.6 — lowest in the missing-set; `model-aliases.generated.md` does not list it as retired or merged — stays queued but unverified; `average.md` Overall 46.6 derived from agent ratings only — lowest among tracked models in dataset). Not deprecated explicitly but described as experimental/sandbox.
- **Specs (from dataset/catalog tracking only — no independent verification for exact ID):** Context 128K (`modelcomp.vercel.app` — 128,000 total); modalities text in / text out; reasoning not explicitly confirmed; tool-calling not explicitly confirmed; model ID / endpoint / weights / price / architecture all listed as "no public model id, endpoint, weights, price or benchmarks" per `modelcomp.vercel.app`. Confirmed absence of verified specs for exact identity.
- **Benchmark verification:** `modelcomp.vercel.app` explicitly states: "Nothing to evaluate — the folder's findings are a self-exclusion." It also notes `Benchmark agreement: 9 figures` but clarifies these are dataset agent-report ratings (`model-queue.md` / agent-rating-based average), not verified independent benchmark registry numbers (`benchmarkregistry.org` / `artificialanalysis.ai` / `benchgap.net` / official vendor benchmark card). The closest verified benchmarks belong to family members (`mai-thinking-1` or `mai-code-1-flash`) but are not verified specifically for `mai-experimental-test` and should not be copied or assumed.
- **No verified independent benchmark numbers for any of the 7 quality dimensions (Tool use, Reasoning, Context window, Multimodal, Coding, Cost efficiency, Overall Score) specifically for exact ID `mai-experimental-test`.** Every category: `no verified public score found` for exact model ID.
- **Twin / exclusion:** No existing `.md` or `.excluded` twin found in folder (`model/mai-experimental-test/` has `average.md`, `meta.json`, other agent findings files — no `Inkling.md` or `.excluded` before this write). `.md.excluded` created as sole file per self-exclusion rule. No deletion of other agent files (only creation of `.excluded` findings file for `STEM: Inkling`).
- **Alias / identity check:** Not listed in `model-aliases.generated.md` (not retired, not merged, not parked, not alias-family). Stays in dataset queue as experimental entry. Not a phantom checkpoint (family members `mai-thinking-1` and `mai-code-1-flash` are fully verified; the experimental slot represents an unverified/test/development entry in the dataset, not a revealed stealth alias or merged duplicate). No identity conflict — just absence of verified identity for exact slot.

